content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth.md:35:sleeve gastrectomy, laparoscopic surgery, keyhole surgery, bariatric surgery, out-of-pocket gap, Medicare rebate, MBS item 31575, private health insurance, hospital cover tier, 12-month waiting period, anaesthetist fee, surgeon's fee, hospital facility fee, BMI eligibility, comorbidities, super release, St John of God Murdoch, excess weight loss, dietitian follow-up, GP referral
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth.md:65:1. **Separate fee types / 4+** — surgeon, hospital, anaesthetist, physician (briefly define what each covers)
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth.md:67:3. **Private cover / Required** — appropriate hospital cover tier needed; note many policies require a higher tier for bariatric procedures
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth.md:73:Explain that there is no one figure because the total is made up of several separate fees billed by different providers. Name the main components: surgeon's fee, anaesthetist's fee, hospital (facility) fee, physician and dietitian fees for assessment and follow-up. Two patients can pay different amounts for the same operation — this is normal in Australian private surgery.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth.md:76:The factors that move the number: the patient's private health insurance policy and what it covers, the level of hospital cover held, whether the waiting period has been served, and the individual's clinical needs. Keep this factual and neutral — don't scare or oversell.
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth.md:87:- Private health funds require an appropriate hospital cover tier that explicitly includes bariatric (weight loss) surgery; many require a higher tier policy; many apply a 12-month waiting period
content-briefs/gastric-sleeve-cost-perth.md:95:2. **Orientation Consultation** — Patient meets the team, discusses whether a sleeve is appropriate; receives a written, itemised cost estimate covering surgeon, anaesthetist and hospital fees at this stage
