content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:178:> Gastric bypass surgery cost in Australia varies depending on your level of private health insurance cover, your surgeon and anaesthetist fees, hospital and theatre charges, and any out-of-pocket gap that applies to your situation. [Medicare item numbers 31572 and 31581](https://www9.health.gov.au/mbs/search.cfm?q=gastric+bypass&Submit=&sopt=S) attract a rebate when eligibility criteria are met, and private health insurance (typically a gold-tier or equivalent policy) covers the hospital and theatre component. Your surgeon's fee for a primary laparoscopic gastric bypass is $6,000 for both insured and uninsured patients, rising to $[X,XXX] for a complex case. For those without private health cover, or where out-of-pocket costs are a concern, superannuation may be accessible as a funding option in certain circumstances, including life-threatening conditions, certain psychiatric conditions, and the management of chronic pain. Financing options such as Zip and TLC are also available for eligible patients. A full breakdown of costs, funding pathways, and pre-surgical clinical fees can be found here.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:180:> Gastric bypass surgery cost in Perth varies by surgeon, anaesthetist, hospital and private health cover. The practice can provide an itemised estimate before you decide; Medicare, private health cover or early release of superannuation may contribute in some circumstances, subject to eligibility, policy terms and applicable rules. See the [Medicare and private health cover guide](/medicare-private-health-cover) for funding detail.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:226:> The Obesity Surgery WA surgical team performs gastric bypass surgery in Perth at three locations: [Mount Private Hospital](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [The Park Private Hospital](https://www.tpph.com.au/), and [Waikiki Private Hospital](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/). Pre- and post-operative (once you’ve been discharged from hospital) consultations take place at Garden City Specialist Centre, Booragoon, and WA Cardiology Centre in Greenfields.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:228:> The Obesity Surgery WA surgical team performs gastric bypass surgery in Perth at the hospital location(s) confirmed by your surgeon. Pre- and post-operative consultations take place at Garden City Specialist Centre in Booragoon and WA Cardiology Centre in Greenfields.
content-reviews/gastric-bypass-perth.md:246:> Expected weight loss: 70-80% of excess weight, clinical average; results vary. Time in surgery: about 120 minutes under general anaesthetic using a keyhole technique. Hospital stay: usually 2-3 nights. Return to most activity: about 3-4 weeks, with light duties often sooner and heavy lifting later.
