content-reviews/summary.md:23:**2. TGA prescription-medicine references (must-fix + a policy decision).** Not just one semaglutide mention: the hub names semaglutide and, with the eligibility page, carries several GLP-1 *class* references. TGA guidance captures direct **and indirect** references to prescription-medicine classes (GLP-1s, "weight-loss injections") in public health-service advertising. The briefs themselves mandate "GLP-1 medical weight management" coverage, so this is a site-wide question — how does the practice want to describe medical weight management? — to settle once (with legal input) and apply to briefs and drafts together.
content-reviews/summary.md:25:**3. Medicare/BMI accuracy + cost certainty (must-fix).** Drafts state "BMI 35+, or 30–35 with conditions" next to MBS item numbers; the MBS wording (explanatory note TN.8.29) is BMI 40+, or 35+ with major comorbidities — lower-BMI pathways must read "may be considered for assessment", never "you may qualify". **Brief-inherited:** the sleeve and bypass briefs mandate the 35/30–35 framing — correct the briefs too. Also: item 31581 (BPD/duodenal switch) cited on the Roux-en-Y page (should be 31572 only); single dollar fees quoted against the briefs' no-single-figure rule, plus a literal "$[X,XXX]" placeholder; and absolute insurance claims ("gold-tier… covers/will cover the hospital and theatre component") need policy-, waiting-period- and gap-aware wording.
