   265	surgery performed?</span>**
   266	
   267	<span class="mark">We have consulting rooms in Booragoon and
   268	Greenfields, keeping appointments accessible for patients across Perth
   269	and the south-west. Surgeries are performed at [<u>Mount Private
   270	Hospital</u>](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [<u>The Park Private
   271	Hospital</u>](https://www.tpph.com.au/), and [<u>Waikiki Private
   272	Hospital</u>](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/). Once your surgery is
   273	planned, our team will walk you through exactly what to expect, where to
   274	go, and who will be involved at every stage, so there are no surprises
   275	on the day.</span>
   276	
   277	<span class="mark">**5. How do I know which pathway is right for me?  **
   278	You probably won't know until you've had a proper assessment, and that's
   279	entirely normal. The right pathway depends on your BMI, health history,
   280	existing conditions, weight loss goals, and what you're willing to
   281	commit to long term. There is no universal answer, which is why we take
   282	the time to understand your individual situation before making any
   283	recommendations. Your first consultation is designed to give you a clear
   284	picture, with no pressure to decide on the day.</span>
   285	
   286	<span class="mark">**6. Will my weight loss be permanent?  **
   287	Weight loss surgery and medical weight management can both produce
   288	significant, lasting results, but no pathway is entirely passive.
   289	Long-term success depends on the habits and support built around
   290	treatment, and some weight regain over time *is* possible if those
   291	aren't maintained. Our team stays involved well beyond your initial
   292	treatment, adjusting your care as your needs change. The goal is
   293	sustainable results over the long term, not just weight loss in the
   294	short term.</span>
   295	
   296	<span class="mark">**7. Do I need a GP referral to be seen?  **
   297	A referral isn't required to make an enquiry or book a consultation, but
   298	having one is worthwhile. It allows Medicare rebates to apply to your
   299	specialist consultation fee, reducing your out-of-pocket cost for the
   300	appointment. It also ensures your clinician has your relevant medical
   301	history from the outset. If you don't yet have a referral, our team can
   302	advise you on next steps when you get in touch.</span>

