    39	### **<span class="mark">Weight loss surgery in Perth: everything you need to know</span>**
    40	
    41	<span class="mark">  
    42	If you have spent years trying to lose weight and keep it off, you are
    43	not the problem, and you are not alone. Obesity Surgery WA is a
    44	specialist team of surgeons, physicians, dietitians, and exercise
    45	physiologists who have been supporting weight loss in Perth for over 20
    46	years. We work with you to explore your options and decide the best way
    47	forward for *you*. Whether that is a non-surgical weight loss program or
    48	a surgical alternative, we meet you exactly where you are.</span>
    49	
    50	### <span class="mark">**What we mean by weight loss surgery (and why it is only part of the picture)**  Weight loss surgery, also called bariatric surgery, is a group of procedures that change the size or function of your stomach and/or digestive system to help you eat less and feel full sooner. The most common procedures we perform in our Perth weight loss clinics are the gastric sleeve (‘sleeve gastrectomy’) and the gastric bypass, with the adjustable gastric band a viable option for some people. These are all well established procedures with long track records of weight loss success in Australia.</span>
    51	
    52	<span class="mark">Surgery is not the only pathway forward. Because
    53	obesity is a medical condition — not a willpower failure — the right
    54	treatment looks different for every person. Options range from GLP-1
    55	medications and structured very low calorie diets, to dietitian-led
    56	nutrition support, exercise guidance, endoscopic procedures, and
    57	surgery.</span>
    58	
    59	<span class="mark">Obesity Surgery WA is not purely a surgical practice.
    60	We are an in-house team of physicians, surgeons, and allied health
    61	practitioners who treat overweight and obesity as the medical conditions
    62	they are, working together to adapt your care as your needs change over
    63	time.</span>
    64	
    65	<span class="mark">This page is here to help you understand what's
    66	available, so that when you're ready, you can make a confident, informed
    67	decision about what’s right for you.</span>
    68	
    69	| <span class="mark">From GLP-1 medications and structured diet programs through to sleeve, bypass, and band procedures, the weight loss treatment spectrum is broader than most people realise. Many patients move through it over time, and there is no single correct starting point.</span> |
    70	|----|
    71	
    72	### **<span class="mark">Who is eligible for weight loss surgery in Australia?</span>**
    73	
    74	| You may be eligible for weight loss surgery if you have a BMI of 40 or higher, or 35 or higher with a weight-related health condition such as type 2 diabetes or high blood pressure, and where diet and exercise alone have not produced long-term results. Medical weight management options including GLP-1s may be suitable if you have a BMI of 30 or higher. |
    75	|----|
    76	
    77	**<span class="mark">Eligibility for weight loss surgery generally
    78	includes:</span>**
    79	
    80	- <span class="mark">BMI 40+: surgery is generally an appropriate option
   250	health history, goals, and personal preference, and is something we work
   251	through with you.</span>
   252	
   253	<span class="mark">**3. Do I really need to see a dietitian, or can I
   254	just have the procedure?  **
   255	Dietitian involvement is an important part of the process, not an
   256	optional add-on. Before surgery, a dietitian helps prepare your body and
   257	set realistic expectations. After surgery, they guide you through the
   258	staged return to eating and help you build the habits that support
   259	long-term results. Patients who engage with dietitian support
   260	consistently achieve better outcomes, and because our dietitians are
   261	in-house, they can work closely with your surgeon throughout your
   262	care.</span>
   263	
   264	**<span class="mark">4. Where are your Perth clinics, and where is
   265	surgery performed?</span>**
   266	
   267	<span class="mark">We have consulting rooms in Booragoon and
   268	Greenfields, keeping appointments accessible for patients across Perth
   269	and the south-west. Surgeries are performed at [<u>Mount Private
   270	Hospital</u>](https://mountprivatehospital.com.au), [<u>The Park Private
   271	Hospital</u>](https://www.tpph.com.au/), and [<u>Waikiki Private
   272	Hospital</u>](https://waikikiprivate.com.au/). Once your surgery is
   273	planned, our team will walk you through exactly what to expect, where to
   274	go, and who will be involved at every stage, so there are no surprises
   275	on the day.</span>
   276	
   277	<span class="mark">**5. How do I know which pathway is right for me?  **
   278	You probably won't know until you've had a proper assessment, and that's
