docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md-341-  > - [**Gastric bypass (Roux-en-Y)**](/gastric-bypass-perth): changes stomach size and how food passes through the small intestine. It has procedure-specific nutritional requirements and risks; your surgeon can explain why it may or may not be appropriate for your circumstances.
docs/oswa/content-review-2026-07/review/bariatric-surgery-perth.md-342-  > - [**Mini gastric bypass (one anastomosis bypass)**](/mini-gastric-bypass): a bypass variation that creates a single connection between the stomach and small intestine. The surgeon can explain its technical features, risks, follow-up needs and whether it is appropriate for your circumstances.
