--
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-74-- Para 3: Introduce the team composition — not just surgeons; also physicians who manage the medical side of weight, and specialist dietitians whose support is central to the care plan. Whoever the patient sees first, they are stepping into a team that can move them along the spectrum of care as their needs change.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-75-- Para 4: State the aim of the page plainly — to help the reader understand the full range of options so they can make an informed decision, rather than feeling pushed toward any single one.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:76:- Closing comparison note (below paragraphs): Give the reader a quick mental model of the spectrum: medical management (GLP-1 medication, very low calorie diet, dietitian support) at one end, surgical procedures (sleeve, bypass, band) at the other. Acknowledge that many people move between them over time, and there is no single correct starting point.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-77-
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-78-### Eligibility section
--
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-109-- Intro paragraph: Acknowledge that every option on the spectrum carries its own considerations. Frame this as a genuine service to the reader — the team will not pretend otherwise. Medications have side effects. Very low calorie diets need supervision. Surgery is a significant step with real risks and recovery. The clinician should explain how these considerations relate to the reader's medical situation before any commitment.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-110-- Risk bullets to address (one sentence each):
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:111:  - GLP-1 medications can cause nausea, digestive symptoms and other side effects; not suitable for everyone
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-112-  - Very low calorie diets require supervision and are not designed as a permanent eating pattern
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-113-  - Surgical procedures carry risks including bleeding, infection, leaks, blood clots and anaesthetic reactions
--
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-145-- AHPRA/TGA: no testimonials, no before/after claims, no guaranteed outcomes
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-146-- MBS surgical threshold: state BMI 40+ or BMI 35+ with a major co-morbidity as assessment guidance; BMI below 35 does not meet that MBS threshold. Do not present a lower-BMI statement as surgical eligibility.
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md:147:- GLP-1/medical-weight-management advertising policy is pending: use active-ingredient/class names only (semaglutide, liraglutide or GLP-1), never brand names, and verify the final TGA/legal position before publication
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-148-- Voice: plain-language, empathetic, direct; avoid hype; this page is the broadest entry point and the reader may be at their most uncertain and guarded
content-briefs/weight-loss-surgery-perth.md-149-- Reader: a Perth adult at the beginning of their research, possibly BMI 27–35, may not know the word "bariatric", may feel shame or exhaustion — the page must normalise the conversation before it can sell it
